    {
      "id": "UgypcIyUZeZQX9-LAa94AaABAg",
      "author": "@Chansurya7",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_njGmxKfoPrBMaI_BcpyasarYRb-fAoAoQbz4AUVTUbPx-Uvg-WVnjh5erCqOgSOACzYA=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "I survived 2.8 years of little food during the Khmer Rouge genocide.  They gave us about 1 lb of rice, then made to rice soup fed 20 to 30 people a day, and millions people starved to death, and everyone ate anything move.",
      "likeCount": 12,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-30T18:16:43Z",
      "replyCount": 4,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgypcIyUZeZQX9-LAa94AaABAg.Aa8dWyIt-8qAaQOd8igGQt",
          "author": "@Chansurya7",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_njGmxKfoPrBMaI_BcpyasarYRb-fAoAoQbz4AUVTUbPx-Uvg-WVnjh5erCqOgSOACzYA=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "​@TravelToFacts I was about 10 years old back then.  I looked back 10 years ago to the genocide period, I feel like I was trained by heaven to survive.  I climb on tree to watch the farm/garden tenders before I go in the grown area to steal my grown food to feed my siblings. I was like the father to them.  They killed us if they caught. We pick weeds & cook at night, my siblings go 20 meters around the house to watch if they see anyone coming, then they'll make a loud voice for cooker to know of the situation, so we can put off fire and hide the food. We ate grasshoppers, weeds, little crabs, lizards, etc. to survive.  If they don’t know how to do it for these years, they starve to death. Millions killed or starved to death. No food, we were so skinny; we could see eye socket about 1” deep into the skull.  I never thought about getting sick, die, or anything else back then.  I just eat what I can find and go on from day to day, then I know that I am hungry for sure.  Hungry that drove me to find food at any risk.  Smartness is the strength to survive through that inhumane period.",
          "likeCount": 1,
          "publishedAt": "2026-09-06T15:44:13Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "UgypcIyUZeZQX9-LAa94AaABAg.Aa8dWyIt-8qAaQDtpfsQDE",
          "author": "@TravelToFacts",
